**CM5 drop-in compatibility — what the FAQ actually covers.** Radxa's CM5 FAQ documents **8** functional changes, and its subject is **replacing a CM3 with a CM5 on a CM3-derived baseboard** — not running a CM5 on a Raspberry Pi CM4 carrier. Documented: no SPI flash; no 3.5 mm audio (needs an external codec); eDP pins 15/17/21/23/27/29/33/35 unsupported; USB2_HOST3 doesn't exist; MIPI limited to 2-lane. The **only** item in the FAQ that concerns a Raspberry Pi carrier is that **microSD boot on the RPi CM4 IO board requires pin 90 of the third connector to be grounded**.

[X] **Radxa's two hard warnings, quoted exactly.** On the CM3 IO board: *"Can Radxa CM5 be used on Radxa CM3 IO board — No, as the 3 pins (94/96/98) (USB_5V_IN) of the current CM3 + Radxa CM3 IO board are connected to 5V, while CM5 is GPIO."* And on custom CM3 baseboards that tie those pins to 5 V: *"…then cannot replace with CM5, otherwise the board will be damaged."*


